0..71 Comment "// The holders of the roles of inductive-recursive definitions, with an"
72..129 Comment "// eliminator that departs from the canonical eliminator."
130..132 Comment "//"
133..211 Comment "// The eliminator\'s own fixpoint opens no stage, so the stage order refuses no"
212..281 Comment "// call of it. Its holder must answer the canonical eliminator, or an"
282..335 Comment "// eliminator that never answers could take the role."
336..338 Comment "//"
339..410 Comment "// The checker compares the eliminator with the canonical eliminator at"
411..488 Comment "// `intro(x)`. Only the holder unfolds there. This eliminator calls itself on"
489..562 Comment "// its own value, so its answer never reads to a normal form. The checker"
563..577 Comment "// refuses it."
578..580 Comment "//"
581..657 Comment "// - see: `model/universe/ir-codes.gandr` — the eliminator of the family a"
658..717 Comment "//   signature defines, admitted, with its computation rule"
718..793 Comment "// - see: `pathological/universe/ir-decoder.gandr` — a decoder that calls"
794..831 Comment "//   itself on its own value, refused"
